# CVEs with no available fix in Debian Bookworm as of 2026-07-06.
# Reviewed: apt-get upgrade is run at build time so any released patch is applied.
# These packages can't simply be removed — libtinfo6/ncurses are bash pre-deps,
# perl-base is marked essential, and libsqlite3-0/zlib1g back the Python stdlib.
# Re-evaluate each entry when status changes from affected/fix_deferred/will_not_fix.

# zlib1g: integer overflow in zipOpenNewFileInZip4_6 — Debian marked will_not_fix
# Impact: only reachable via crafted ZIP files; agentbox does not process user-supplied ZIPs
CVE-2023-45853

# libsqlite3-0: memory corruption / overflows — no Debian fix available
# Impact: the running service uses Postgres, not SQLite (SQLite is test-only and
# tests don't ship in the runtime image), so this code path isn't exercised at runtime
CVE-2025-7458
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# ncurses: buffer overflow — no Debian fix available (status: affected)
CVE-2025-69720

# gzip: global buffer overflow in the LZH decompression path — no Debian fix
# available (status: affected, reviewed 2026-07-06)
# Impact: only triggered by decompressing crafted LZH archives; agentbox never
# invokes gzip on user-supplied input, let alone LZH archives. gzip is
# priority:required in Debian so it can't be removed from the image.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1: symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl functions — no
# Debian fix available (status: affected, reviewed 2026-07-06)
# Impact: requires a local attacker pre-placing symlinks while a privileged
# process manipulates ACLs; the container runs as a fixed non-root user, has no
# untrusted local users, and agentbox never calls ACL functions. libacl1 is a
# hard dependency of coreutils so it can't be removed.
CVE-2026-54369

# perl-base: multiple CVEs — fix_deferred or affected (no released Debian patch)
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48959
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-9538
